---
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>About StackVersus — Kinetic Benchmark Engine</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Learn how StackVersus delivers unbiased, data-driven software comparisons and developer architecture benchmarks." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;600;700&family=Syne:wght@700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
      :root {
        --z-black: #060707;
        --z-card: rgba(14, 16, 15, 0.72);
        --z-card-hover: rgba(22, 26, 24, 0.85);
        --z-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
        --z-lime: #22E576;
        --z-lime-glow: rgba(34, 229, 118, 0.35);
        --z-coral: #FF385C;
        --z-text: #F2F2F2;
        --z-muted: #8E928E;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
      body {
        font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        background-color: var(--z-black);
        color: var(--z-text);
        min-height: 100vh;
        padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 40px) 20px 80px;
      }
      .container {
        max-width: 840px;
        margin: 0 auto;
      }
      .back-btn {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
        font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        color: #ffffff;
        text-decoration: none;
        padding: 8px 20px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: rgba(14, 18, 16, 0.8);
        border: 1px solid var(--z-border);
        transition: all 0.25s ease;
        margin-bottom: 32px;
      }
      .back-btn:hover {
        background: var(--z-lime);
        color: #000000;
        box-shadow: 0 0 18px var(--z-lime-glow);
        transform: translateX(-4px);
      }
      h1 {
        font-family: 'Syne', sans-serif;
        font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
        font-weight: 800;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #ffffff;
      }
      .glass-panel {
        background: var(--z-card);
        border: 1px solid var(--z-border);
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px);
        line-height: 1.7;
        backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
      }
      h2 {
        font-family: 'Syne', sans-serif;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        color: var(--z-lime);
        margin: 32px 0 14px;
      }
      p { margin-bottom: 16px; color: #dcdcdc; font-size: 1rem; }
      ul { padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 18px; color: #dcdcdc; }
      li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
      
      /* Distinct Callout Box for Affiliate Disclosure */
      .disclosure-box {
        margin: 36px 0 20px;
        padding: 24px 28px;
        background: rgba(10, 14, 12, 0.85);
        border: 1px solid rgba(34, 229, 118, 0.2);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--z-lime);
        border-radius: 12px;
        scroll-margin-top: 40px;
      }
      .disclosure-box h2 {
        margin-top: 0;
        color: #ffffff;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/" class="back-btn">← Back to Main Arena</a>
      <h1>About StackVersus</h1>
      <div class="glass-panel">
        <p>
          StackVersus is an independent developer intelligence platform engineered to eliminate analysis paralysis when evaluating cloud tools, modern databases, and production software infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
          Choosing between developer stacks, cloud infrastructure providers, and modern SaaS tools usually requires wading through marketing hype and vague pricing tiers. StackVersus audits and standardizes direct head-to-head comparisons focusing strictly on architectural fit, developer experience, and cost curves at scale.
        </p>

        <h2>Benchmarking Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          Every comparison in our matrix is cross-evaluated across four core pillars:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Architecture & Runtime:</strong> Evaluated on compute footprint, cold start latencies, memory utilization, connection pooling limits, and self-hosting escape hatches.</li>
          <li><strong>Developer Experience (DX):</strong> Setup friction, CLI ergonomics, SDK ergonomics across TypeScript/Go/Python, and migration complexity.</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent Cost Audits:</strong> Real-world monthly estimates accounting for hidden egress bandwidth fees, seat minimums, and compute overages.</li>
          <li><strong>Multi-Agent Verification:</strong> Technical consistency scored across Google Gemini, Meta LLaMA 3.3, and verified open-source documentation.</li>
        </ul>

        <!-- Targeted Anchor for Footer Link -->
        <div class="disclosure-box" id="disclosure">
          <h2>Affiliate Disclosure & Editorial Independence</h2>
          <p>
            StackVersus is reader-supported. Some links on our comparison tables and action buttons are affiliate tracking links, meaning we may earn a referral commission if you subscribe to a paid plan at no additional cost to you.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            However, our rankings, pros/cons, and technical assessments are generated using objective criteria and verified architectural specs. They are never influenced, altered, or dictated by commercial affiliate partnerships.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Contact & Editorial Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Notice an outdated pricing tier, changed rate limit, or new SDK release? Send correction details directly to our research pipeline at <strong style="color: var(--z-lime); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;">team@stackversus.pages.dev</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>